k[t]`).\n- `SWAP a b`: The masks at positions `a` and `b` are exchanged.\n\nStarting with `mask = 0xFFFFFFFFFF` (all 40 bits set to 1) and pushing it through the 299 operations of the `OUTER` block, we yield the following mask bits (from $x[39]$ down to $x[0]$):\n`1111 0011 0010 1100 0011 0010 1010 1111 0011 1101` in binary.\n\nThis binary string translates to `0xF32C32AF3D` in hexadecimal, which equals `1044418572093` in decimal. Choosing an offset of 0 maps this alternating parity sequence directly to the valid colors {0, 1}.\n\n<answer>{\"mask\":1044418572093,\"offset\":0}</answer>", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 97.85, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "hard", "escalation_round": 0}
